  <!-- ===== MISSION CARDS ===== -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <span class="section-label">What We Do</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Our Mission in Action</h2>
        <div class="divider divider--center"></div>
        <p class="section-subtitle">
          Three pillars — education, water, and community — guide everything we do
          for the South Sudanese people here and in East Africa.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid card-grid--3">

        <div class="card fade-up __aw-card visible">
          <div class="card__icon-band card__icon-band--gold"></div>
          <div class="card__body">
            <div class="card__icon card__icon--gold"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"></path><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"></path></svg></div>
            <h3 class="card__title">Education</h3>
            <p class="card__text">
              Ayaa Senior Secondary School in Magwi Center, South Sudan serves
              200+ students from Senior One through Senior Four. Named after
              Simon's mother, the school transforms lives through learning.
            </p>
            <a href="school.html" class="card__link">Learn about the school →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card fade-up __aw-card visible">
          <div class="card__icon-band card__icon-band--blue"></div>
          <div class="card__body">
            <div class="card__icon card__icon--blue"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2.69l5.66 5.66a8 8 0 1 1-11.31 0z"></path></svg></div>
            <h3 class="card__title">Safe Water</h3>
            <p class="card__text">
              In partnership with Louisville nonprofit WaterStep, we are bringing
              clean, safe water to the school and surrounding village — ending
              generations of bilharzia and waterborne disease from the River Ayii.
            </p>
            <a href="programs.html" class="card__link">See our programs →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card fade-up __aw-card visible">
          <div class="card__icon-band card__icon-band--green"></div>
          <div class="card__body">
            <div class="card__icon card__icon--green"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"></path><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path></svg></div>
            <h3 class="card__title">Community Support</h3>
            <p class="card__text">
              Right here in Louisville, Kentucky, AYAA supports South Sudanese
              immigrants and refugees with resources, connection, and advocacy —
              helping our community thrive in their adopted home.
            </p>
            <a href="programs.html" class="card__link">Get involved →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    <p class="" style="line-height: 1.8; margin: 0.75rem 0px; cursor: text;">cvvcvcv</p></div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== SIMON'S STORY TEASER ===== -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="story-grid">
        <div class="story__visual fade-up visible">
          <div class="founder-portrait">
            <img src="SImon.jpg" alt="Simon Ottaviano, Founder and President of AYAA South Sudanese Community Organization">
            <div class="founder-portrait__badge">
              <div class="founder-portrait__badge-name">Simon Ottaviano</div>
              <div class="founder-portrait__badge-title">Founder &amp; President, AYAA</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-up visible">
          <span class="story__label">The Founder's Journey</span>
          <h2 class="story__title">From Magwi to Louisville — A Story of Sacrifice and Service</h2>
          <div class="divider"></div>
          <p class="story__text">
            Simon Ottaviano was born in Magwi County, South Sudan — Acholi territory in Eastern Equatoria —
            the son of Ottaviano Oyat, the Paramount Chief of the Acholi people in South Sudan.
            When civil war tore through his homeland, Simon fled to the United States in 1994.
          </p>
          <p class="story__text">
            He served six years in the U.S. Army, earned an MBA from Sullivan University in 2008,
            spent 12 years at Anthem Blue Cross and Blue Shield, and became a licensed REALTOR.
            But through it all, he never forgot Magwi.
          </p>
          <p class="story__text">
            In 2022, Simon made the ultimate sacrifice: he sold his house and cashed out his 401(k)
            to build a school back home — the Ayaa Senior Secondary School, named after his mother.
          </p>
          <a href="about.html" class="btn btn--primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Read Simon's Full Story</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== ACTIVE CAMPAIGN HIGHLIGHT ===== -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="urgency-alert">
        <div class="urgency-alert__icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"></path><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"></polyline></svg></div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="urgency-alert__title">Urgent: Girls' Dormitory Campaign</h3>
          <p class="urgency-alert__text">
            Every school day, hundreds of girls walk 4 to 5 miles each way to reach Ayaa Senior Secondary School —
            crossing dangerous terrain, exposed to risk. A dormitory will keep them safe and in school.
            <strong>Your donation can change this.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="school.html" class="btn btn--outline-dark" style="flex-shrink: 0; margin-left: auto;">Learn More</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  <p class="" style="line-height: 1.8; margin: 0.75rem 0px; cursor: text;">Your text here — click to edit</p></section>

